{"title":"Career roadmap · Stock Market Analyst","role":"Stock Market Analyst","summary":"A Stock Market Analyst researches companies, industries and financial markets to evaluate securities, identify investment opportunities, assess risks and produce investment recommendations or research reports.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Com (Bachelor of Commerce)","Course":"Financial Markets (BFM) / Banking & Insurance (BBI)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"B.Com – Financial Markets (BFM) / Banking & Insurance (BBI) is strongly aligned, particularly when the student builds additional capability in accounting, valuation, financial modelling, economics, statistics and market research."},{"type":"note","label":"Career-route check","text":"Direct alignment, but analyst roles can be competitive. A strong route is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Com BFM/BBI","Equity Research/Investment Research Intern","Research Analyst Trainee","Equity/Stock Market Analyst","Senior Analyst","Portfolio/Research Leadership"]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"A research analyst role in regulated financial markets can have qualification, certification and registration requirements depending on the exact role and employer. Check current SEBI requirements before providing regulated investment recommendations."}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career objective"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build accounting, markets, valuation, Excel and research skills; enter equity/market research"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Specialise in sectors such as banking, technology, pharma, FMCG, energy or industrials"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Progress to Senior Analyst, Sector Lead, Portfolio Analyst or Investment Strategist"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Move toward Research Head, Portfolio Manager, Investment Strategist or senior investment lea